      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Home Depot is a defendant under any reasonable construction of that term and, in fact, that's our only role in this case. We're just a defendant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1471",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae2963f25dfcb0842ea20f6cda794e50a4e519d5fb10d2d68bc3ea020fef8b18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae2963f25dfc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm not quite sure, putting this outside the class action setting, generally, all defendants have to agree to removal and with some other limitations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Barnette",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1471",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae2963f25dfcb0842ea20f6cda794e50a4e519d5fb10d2d68bc3ea020fef8b18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae2963f25dfc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BARNETTE: Your Honor, again, I would just point the Court to Rule 3 of the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure, which says a civil action is commenced by filing a complaint"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1471",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae2963f25dfcb0842ea20f6cda794e50a4e519d5fb10d2d68bc3ea020fef8b18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae2963f25dfc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But what you're arguing is not based on the language, not based on the term \"original jurisdiction\" in 1441. It's based on the well-pleaded complaint rule. Am I right on that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1471",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae2963f25dfcb0842ea20f6cda794e50a4e519d5fb10d2d68bc3ea020fef8b18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae2963f25dfc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Since when are law review articles peer reviewed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1471",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae2963f25dfcb0842ea20f6cda794e50a4e519d5fb10d2d68bc3ea020fef8b18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae2963f25dfc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Who are they -- who are they reviewed by?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1471",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ae2963f25dfcb0842ea20f6cda794e50a4e519d5fb10d2d68bc3ea020fef8b18",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ae2963f25dfc-0002-0002",
